Chapter: F32StorageArm
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceEffect

 The positive arm for f32 storage. Bindings are array<i32>, so an f32 element
 crosses them by bitcast (WgslSpec.md 16.8, bitcast<T> reinterprets the bits):

   device-load-f32 b i        bitcast<f32>(b[i])
   device-store-f32 b i v     b[i] = bitcast<i32>(v)

 fs-copy moves a value through both and must hand back the same 32 bits;
 fs-axpy must compute on the float, which a conversion in place of a bitcast
 (i32(x), f32(b[i])) gets wrong for every input that is not an integer.

 We say:

Section: Kernels

  fs-copy : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  fs-copy (xb) (yb) (gid) = device-store-f32 yb gid (device-load-f32 xb gid)

  fs-axpy : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  fs-axpy (xb) (yb) (gid) = device-store-f32 yb gid (device-load-f32 xb gid * 2.5 + 1.0)

  fs-copy-approx : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  fs-copy-approx (xb) (yb) (gid) = device-store-approx yb gid (device-load-approx xb gid)

 Two guarded stores from one thread: y[2 gid] = x[gid] and y[2 gid + 1] =
 -x[gid], each only while its index is under n.

  fs-two-guarded : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  fs-two-guarded (xb) (yb) (n) (gid) = act
   a <- (if gid * 2 < n then device-store-f32 yb (gid * 2) (device-load-f32 xb gid) else 0)
   b <- (if gid * 2 + 1 < n then device-store-f32 yb (gid * 2 + 1) (0.0 - device-load-f32 xb gid) else 0)
   0
  end

  fs-const-approx : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  fs-const-approx (xb) (yb) (gid) = device-store-approx yb gid (device-load-approx xb gid * bits-to-real-approx #BF000000 + real-approx-from-int 3)
